{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Change 2 (push.py recovery-cluster split) pushed to Gerrit as change 1753, stacked on 1752 (Change 1) and 1751 (Change 3).\n\nResult: push.py 800->524 LOC; new push_recovery.py 366 LOC (both in-band). Extracted the 8-function recovery cluster + _PUSH_MERGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT using the core: ModuleType late-binding pattern (per _ref_lock_push.py precedent) so the ~25 push._git monkeypatch sites still intercept. push.py retains old-signature delegating shims for _recover_dirty_merge and _recover_non_fast_forward, and re-exports the remaining members so push.<symbol> access and _resolve_conflicted_apply.__doc__ survive.\n\nVerification: ruff + mypy clean; module-size gate clean; import smoke test (shims callable, doc preserved, constant intact) OK. Monkeypatch-sensitive suites pass: test_push_strict, test_push_strict_happy, test_epoch_guard_matrix, test_push_shared_stash_2fa6, test_get_rotation_heldout. The 10 test_commit_and_push_tickets_branch_heldout failures are a pre-existing environmental 'safe.bareRepository is explicit' git-config error at test setup — confirmed identical on clean origin/main (a79ed876b0), not caused by this change.\n\nGerrit changes now open: 1751 (Change 3), 1752 (Change 1), 1753 (Change 2). Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 on each before submit + close."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786665872056170001,"uuid":"3c0375cf-912a-43f7-9ef5-3e1c7def29c4"}